      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the Electoral College was historically designed to balance federalism with popular sovereignty, its rigid disproportionality now systematically disenfractages millions of American voters and distorts the will of the electorate. By awarding disproportionate political power to specific regions while rendering vast swaths of the population politically irrelevant, the system fundamentally undermines the democratic principle of \"one person, one vote.\" As the 2020 election demonstrated, this legacy mechanism encourages a dysfunctional two-party duopoly and prevents the right-wing minority from ever unifying a majority to elect their preferred candidate. Ultimately, clinging to this anachronistic framework not only contravenes the core ideals of modern democracy but also perpetuates a fractured political reality that must be urgently reformed.",
